; the browser's window as a Model-View-Update program
; (docs/architecture.md): Window_model (the state and the messages),
; Window_layout (the model read: where each part is, what is under the
; pointer), Window_tabs (the model changed: a tab's settings, one
; changed, opened, closed; scroll, zoom, the profile), Window_update
; (what each message does) and Window_view (the shapes). src/main's
; MiniChrome.ml runs it, on either of the Playground's platforms.
(library
 (name browser_window)
 (wrapped false)
 (flags (:standard -open Network)) ; ours, not the Playground's (libs/network/dune)
 (modules_without_implementation window_model) ; types alone
 (libraries
   caps ; the network and the profile's file, handed down by main
   tiny_libs.core network
   mini_opti ; the same view for the same model (Window_view)
   mini_gui ; the chrome's pieces
   lang_html lang_css browser_layout
   browser_url browser_display browser_www browser_dom browser_viewers browser_about browser_chrome
   elm_playground))
